WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:20.000
The United States Army presents the Big Picture, an official report produced for the Armed

00:20.000 --> 00:40.000
Forces and the American people.

01:20.000 --> 01:40.120
This is foolish. I can't sit here forever. No matter how I feel, I've just got to finish

01:40.120 --> 01:48.040
my letter. I've got to write it and hope Mother will understand. Will she really understand?

01:48.040 --> 01:54.180
How well do I know my mother? How well do I actually know her? It seems such a strange

01:54.180 --> 02:01.000
question to be asking myself after all the years we've been so close to each other. That's

02:01.000 --> 02:09.760
the problem. All those years, all those warm, wonderful years. How do I write what I have

02:09.760 --> 02:15.060
to say without spoiling any part of it? How do I tell her that her own hopes can't be

02:15.060 --> 02:23.400
realized yet, only because they don't happen to coincide with mine? How? Am I being selfish?

02:23.400 --> 02:32.360
Am I thinking only of myself? I don't know. How does one judge? All I know is that somehow

02:32.360 --> 02:40.720
I must write what I feel, explain what my decision means to me, and hope she will understand.

02:40.720 --> 02:45.360
Perhaps it would be better if I asked for special leave so I could sit with her and

02:45.360 --> 02:51.560
explain. No, it would still involve my finding the right words. And how did that poem I learned

02:51.560 --> 03:05.800
in college go? Words are but such empty thanks for all the good you've wrought. Dear Mother,

03:05.800 --> 03:11.000
I know how anxiously you've been waiting to hear from me about my decision, and I am sorry

03:11.000 --> 03:16.280
that it's taken me this long to make up my mind. It was really not an easy decision to

03:16.280 --> 03:22.840
make. I feel my biggest problem is not just telling you what I've decided to do, but in

03:22.840 --> 03:28.800
explaining things so you will believe that I am doing what is best for both of us. In

03:28.800 --> 03:34.280
thinking about it now, it seems to me, Mother, that while I've always told you about my experiences

03:34.280 --> 03:39.600
as an Army nurse, I have never actually expressed to you what these experiences have come to

03:39.600 --> 03:52.520
mean to me and why. Perhaps the best way to start is to try to recall for you all that

03:52.520 --> 03:57.280
has happened and passed through my mind these last few days, beginning with a meeting I

03:57.280 --> 04:02.600
had with Colonel Leemark. You remember her. You met her when you visited me here last

04:02.600 --> 04:09.000
Thanksgiving. And next to you, Mother, she's one of the most considerate persons I've ever

04:09.000 --> 04:20.640
known. I hope you understand, Ruth, that I'm obliged to call you in this way and ask what

04:20.640 --> 04:26.840
you've decided to do. I'm sure they think I'm pretty remiss in my duties as Chief of

04:26.840 --> 04:31.480
the Nursing Service here at the hospital for not pressing you for a definite answer long

04:31.480 --> 04:38.320
before this. I know, Colonel Leemark. I'm sure they do. Ruth, we can't hold up your

04:38.320 --> 04:44.280
decision any longer. Regulations say you should have given me your answer weeks ago. I've

04:44.280 --> 04:50.960
run out of excuses. I know. And I'm sorry. Well, actually, it's not regulations I'm as

04:50.960 --> 04:55.480
concerned about as I am about you and your connection with the Corps. Ruth, you know

04:55.480 --> 05:01.280
how we feel about you, how much we think you've grown professionally and as an individual.

05:01.280 --> 05:05.600
I, for one, have made no secret about how far I think someone with your interests and

05:05.600 --> 05:13.760
capabilities can go as an Army nurse. I'd hate to see us lose you. Must we? I don't

05:13.760 --> 05:20.000
know. I just haven't been able to believe that my answer depends upon me alone. And

05:20.000 --> 05:26.680
I haven't been able to do anything about it. I'm sure that sounds foolish. And I'm just

05:26.680 --> 05:31.560
as sure that if there is anything troubling you, there's undoubtedly a sound reason for

05:31.560 --> 05:37.760
it. I've always found there's nothing like a good, sympathetic listener whom you trust

05:37.760 --> 05:46.120
to help settle the questions on one's mind. Or am I prying? Oh, no, of course not. You

05:46.120 --> 05:50.600
can't imagine how many times I've thought about coming to you. It's just that I was

05:50.600 --> 05:55.720
afraid you'd think I was behaving like a foolish little girl who'd forgotten to grow up. I

05:55.720 --> 06:01.720
think you know me better than to worry about anything like that. You know what happened

06:01.720 --> 06:07.040
the last time I was home on leave? My mother had taken all the money that I'd been sending

06:07.040 --> 06:12.920
her to use for herself, saved it, and gone out and bought me the best car she could find

06:12.920 --> 06:20.920
as a surprise. Is that so bad? No. At least not until you know the other things. From

06:20.920 --> 06:26.640
the time my father died, when I was just six years old, my mother has worked and struggled

06:26.640 --> 06:34.000
to make certain I had everything I needed. No one knows how much she sacrificed for me.

06:34.000 --> 06:39.320
Mother never went anywhere or did anything without me. And yet she never, ever discouraged

06:39.320 --> 06:45.040
me from doing the things I wanted to do on my own. She must be a wonderful person. Oh,

06:45.040 --> 06:52.080
she is, especially to me. When I talked as a child about wanting to become a nurse, she

06:52.080 --> 06:57.600
not only saw that I finished high school, she put aside enough money to insure my enrollment

06:57.600 --> 07:03.040
at the University School of Nursing. And when I went out and got a job to help out, she

07:03.040 --> 07:08.200
was terribly upset because she was afraid it might interfere with my studies. Things

07:08.200 --> 07:14.960
like that have made me very fond of my mother. But if you were so devoted, I don't understand

07:14.960 --> 07:19.120
how you became involved in the Army Student Nurse Program. You must have known it would

07:19.120 --> 07:24.960
mean separation, at least for a period of time. I brought material about the program

07:24.960 --> 07:30.200
Home from School. Mother saw it. After we talked about it, we both agreed it was the

07:30.200 --> 07:36.400
surest way of my getting something I wanted very much, my bachelor's degree in nursing.

07:36.400 --> 07:41.400
She encouraged me to enroll for two years, even though she knew it meant my being away

07:41.400 --> 07:47.600
after graduation for three years. And now that your required time is almost up, she

07:47.600 --> 07:54.120
wants you to come home? She hasn't said so. She never would. But I can sense it. I can

07:54.120 --> 08:01.120
see it in her eyes that I'm her great achievement in life, her only achievement. She doesn't

08:01.120 --> 08:08.520
mean anything by it. It's just that she's always had so very little. I know that she

08:08.520 --> 08:13.120
would like for me to come home and work in a civilian hospital where she can point to

08:13.120 --> 08:18.720
me with pride as her great achievement in life, something she and I have been able to

08:18.720 --> 08:30.200
do in spite of everything. But what do you want to do, Ruth? I don't know. The need for

08:30.200 --> 08:35.480
nurses in civilian hospitals is as great as in our own Corps. I'm sure you'd find the

08:35.480 --> 08:41.320
same challenges and rewards, but that isn't what you really want, is it, Ruth? How can

08:41.320 --> 08:47.280
I disappoint someone I love, Colonel Leamock? How can I tell someone who's always been so

08:47.280 --> 08:52.240
generous to me that she can't have the one thing in life that might bring her her greatest

08:52.240 --> 09:00.520
happiness? I wish I could answer that, but I can't. At least I do know now what kept

09:00.520 --> 09:09.120
you from making a decision. Ruth, no one can tell you what to do or has the right to. It's

09:09.120 --> 09:14.200
just that like so many of us at some time in our life, you're standing at an important

09:14.200 --> 09:20.120
crossroads. And the sad part about that is that no matter which path you choose, you're

09:20.120 --> 09:25.920
going to bring some happiness and some unhappiness to yourself and everyone else involved. The

09:25.920 --> 09:30.520
only thing to do at a time like this is to try and weigh everything in a kind of mental

09:30.520 --> 09:36.840
scale and then try and select the best possible path. You understand, don't you, Ruth? Yes,

09:36.840 --> 09:41.160
Colonel. You must try and measure what you give up with what you gain, whichever direction

09:41.160 --> 09:47.160
you go, and which is more likely to bring you the greatest possible happiness. And I

09:47.160 --> 09:52.080
have the feeling that whichever makes you happiest would be what your mother herself

09:52.080 --> 10:01.840
would have chosen for you. I'm afraid I haven't been thinking very logically, Colonel. May

10:01.840 --> 10:06.960
I have a little more time? Well, I don't think they'll court-martial me if I give you another

10:06.960 --> 10:13.720
day or two. Thank you, Colonel. And Ruth, even though I said I had no right to take

10:13.720 --> 10:18.240
sides, I hope you don't mind my mentioning again how valuable I think you are to the

10:18.240 --> 10:31.560
Corps. I went to my favorite spot to think, a lovely park near the hospital. Paul and

10:31.560 --> 10:38.640
I always came here when we had something personal to talk or think about. I began by recalling

10:38.640 --> 10:42.940
all the experiences I could remember having since joining the Corps. My thoughts went

10:42.940 --> 10:47.200
back to my graduation from college, which was very exciting, but more thrilling was

10:47.200 --> 10:52.520
my flight to Sam Houston, Texas. I, who had never even been in a plane before, here I

10:52.520 --> 11:02.520
was traveling almost a thousand miles from home. Brooke Army Medical Center and the Medical

11:02.520 --> 11:07.160
Field Service School, where all new medical service people are brought for their introduction

11:07.160 --> 11:13.920
into the Army and the Army family. From the moment you arrive, you begin to feel somehow

11:13.920 --> 11:26.040
that you've embarked on a new and terribly exciting adventure. Everything is so new,

11:26.040 --> 11:34.040
so different, including the clothes you get to wear in the field. And those you wear on

11:34.040 --> 11:38.160
other occasions, clothes that have been so well-fashioned they flatter every girl who

11:38.160 --> 11:43.960
puts them on. And you also begin to realize how good it feels to be an officer in the

11:43.960 --> 11:49.800
United States Army. The Medical Field Service School at Brooke is often called the Army

11:49.800 --> 11:55.200
Medical University. Here you are indoctrinated in the special problems involved in the practice

11:55.200 --> 12:00.760
of Army medicine, and here you begin to appreciate that you have become a member of a large,

12:00.760 --> 12:08.560
important community, dispersed though it is over the country and the world, the Army.

12:08.560 --> 12:13.480
You suddenly begin to have a feeling of pride in yourself and the other nurses you're with,

12:13.480 --> 12:17.880
some from allied nations. You're glad you made nursing your life's work, but you're

12:17.880 --> 12:25.080
happier still to be doing it in the service of your country. Because our national and

12:25.080 --> 12:30.120
civilian defense must always be safeguarded, the Army nurse is given an opportunity to

12:30.120 --> 12:36.440
work under field conditions. Various situations are simulated for the medical staff which

12:36.440 --> 12:41.000
has been brought here, so that each might practice his or her particular skills under

12:41.000 --> 12:47.440
what might be considered trying conditions. Accept that you're constantly aware of the

12:47.440 --> 12:52.780
thought and study that have gone into each piece of field equipment, items carefully

12:52.780 --> 13:02.080
developed for the most difficult kind of surgery, for the care and treatment of patients, as

13:02.080 --> 13:09.040
well as for the comfort and well-being of those whose duty it is to perform these services.

13:09.040 --> 13:13.680
And when the new nurse talks with her newfound friends, she finds that she's not alone in

13:13.680 --> 13:20.240
feeling that this episode of her life is quite romantic. Field nursing is only one phase

13:20.240 --> 13:25.360
of Army nursing, and so while at the medical field service school, the Army nurse observes

13:25.360 --> 13:29.680
and practices her skills under supervision at Brooke Army Medical Center, of which the

13:29.680 --> 13:38.400
service school is a part. This is no small opportunity, for Brooke is one of the largest

13:38.400 --> 13:43.760
military medical installations in the world. You don't realize it at the time, but you've

13:43.760 --> 13:49.520
begun a period of sustained and systematic learning that need never end for an Army nurse.

13:49.520 --> 13:53.800
If you enjoy learning new things all the time, as I do, and having fun along with it, as

13:53.800 --> 14:18.360
everybody does, both come naturally with every Army assignment. You enjoy doing new things.

14:18.360 --> 14:30.680
Many activities you never felt you could afford before. And there are always those dances

14:30.680 --> 14:35.360
at the officers club, where you can relax in the pleasant company of such very nice

14:35.360 --> 14:41.760
people. So I enjoyed every moment at Brooke. Remember how excited I was, Mother, when I

14:41.760 --> 14:47.600
was assigned to Fitzsimmons Hospital in Denver, Colorado? It's said the wise person is one

14:47.600 --> 14:53.120
who knows that the more one learns, the more one realizes there is to learn. At Fitzsimmons,

14:53.120 --> 15:00.040
the truth of this struck me. Although I was still quite fresh out of school, I had been

15:00.040 --> 15:04.980
thinking about myself as a nurse for some time now. But here I had the greatest chance

15:04.980 --> 15:10.760
in the world to discover for myself how much there is to know in the profession of nursing.

15:10.760 --> 15:15.480
And the wonderful thing about being an Army nurse is that your interests, your ambitions

15:15.480 --> 15:21.120
are always encouraged. Every effort is made to place you in contact with all facets of

15:21.120 --> 15:25.960
nursing so you may grow professionally just as far and as fast as your abilities will

15:25.960 --> 15:36.040
take you. Besides general nursing, the Army nurse is instructed in such other areas as

15:36.040 --> 15:45.240
the special care of cardiac surgery patients and the victims of respiratory disorders.

15:45.240 --> 15:49.240
She is taught the use of a great many types of special medical equipment of which the

15:49.240 --> 15:57.840
Army has the latest and finest. She may work with anxious mothers-to-be, assist in the

15:57.840 --> 16:04.440
marvel of bringing a new life into the world, and observe the special joy of parenthood

16:04.440 --> 16:14.640
for the new mother, as well as for the generally disbelieving and bewildered father. The Army

16:14.640 --> 16:23.040
nurse is exposed to pediatrics and the particular medical problems of the very young, to orthopedics

16:23.040 --> 16:29.960
and the most advanced methods for the treatment of every type of injury, as well as those

16:29.960 --> 16:37.240
who have become mentally ill. The learning process never stops. You meet regularly with

16:37.240 --> 16:41.640
those who are more skilled and knowledgeable than yourself so that you may speed your own

16:41.640 --> 16:49.040
development. Attend hospital seminars for detailed instruction in various medical and

16:49.040 --> 16:56.840
clinical problems or the latest facts in medical advancements. Or you may enroll under Army

16:56.840 --> 17:02.040
auspices in a nearby college or university to obtain a degree if you don't have one,

17:02.040 --> 17:09.440
or to work for a higher degree. Yes, the learning process never ends if you don't want it to.

17:09.440 --> 17:13.840
Your total education is further increased by the insight you get of people, what makes

17:13.840 --> 17:19.240
them tick, and by the understanding and appreciation you begin to feel for life's complexities

17:19.240 --> 17:28.440
and some of its seeming miracles. And you give thanks for the fact that you have found

17:28.440 --> 17:33.040
your way to the work you wanted most to do in life, and for the opportunity you've been

17:33.040 --> 17:40.640
given to do it. For the welcome awareness that comes, in the shadows of the night perhaps,

17:40.640 --> 17:45.240
of the special rewards reserved for those charged with the responsibility of restoring

17:45.240 --> 17:56.640
the ill and the injured back to health. But no one expects your growth as an individual

17:56.640 --> 18:01.240
to proceed in only one direction. You are continually encouraged to add to your general

18:01.240 --> 18:06.640
knowledge, your social, physical, and emotional growth, simply because the more you accrue

18:06.640 --> 18:12.640
to your personal assets, the more valuable you become to yourself and the service. And

18:12.640 --> 18:17.840
the beautiful Rocky Mountains, only a short distance away from Fitzsimmons Hospital, provide

18:17.840 --> 18:30.640
the loveliest setting for every interest. The adventurous hikers and lovers of nature.

18:30.640 --> 18:37.840
For the most avid and incurable romanticist. And aren't we all? But my richest professional

18:37.840 --> 18:44.040
experience came with my assignment to Walter Reed Army Hospital, Washington, D.C. Walter

18:44.040 --> 18:50.440
Reed, the hospital of presidents, of statesmen, of army personnel and their families. Internationally

18:50.440 --> 18:55.440
recognized as one of the finest hospitals in the world. And what an opportunity it is

18:55.440 --> 19:00.640
to be stationed here. For here, you find you have entered still another new and exciting

19:00.640 --> 19:06.840
aspect of your professional career. The hospital looks in most respects like hospitals you've

19:06.840 --> 19:15.640
been in before. But a most unusual and significant thing seems to happen to the nurse a short

19:15.640 --> 19:21.540
time after she arrives here. An entirely new vista opens up and she sees herself not simply

19:21.540 --> 19:28.440
as another nurse, but as a vital part of a closely knit, dedicated team. Teamwork is

19:28.440 --> 19:32.640
the watchword of army nursing everywhere. And while you know it exists wherever the

19:32.640 --> 19:40.540
army provides medical services, its full meaning seems to have escaped you until now. Perhaps

19:40.540 --> 19:45.340
it's a symptom of your growing professional maturity. Or it may be the fact that you are

19:45.340 --> 19:51.040
in contact with some of the best trained minds, skilled hands, medical, scientific and technical

19:51.040 --> 19:57.340
specialists to be found anywhere. Whatever the reason, you as an army nurse suddenly

19:57.340 --> 20:02.140
find yourself looking at your patients with an increased confidence, born from the sure

20:02.140 --> 20:10.140
knowledge that you are a part of a creative and excellent team. A team of surgeons and

20:10.140 --> 20:15.040
physicians in every branch of medical science, some internationally recognized leaders in

20:15.040 --> 20:23.240
their particular field. Scientists and researchers in chemistry, biochemistry and many other disciplines,

20:23.240 --> 20:28.340
all seeking to pull back the veil from the unknown in order to save more lives and increase

20:28.340 --> 20:34.840
the effectiveness of our medical service. There are nurses who are teachers of other

20:34.840 --> 20:42.640
nurses. Technicians operating special equipment and performing special services without which

20:42.640 --> 20:50.540
no modern hospital could hope to operate effectively and efficiently today. Physical therapists

20:50.540 --> 20:58.440
utilizing the latest techniques to restore the functions of injured limbs and body tissues.

20:58.440 --> 21:06.440
Occupational therapists skillfully guiding patients back to full and useful lives. Dietitians

21:06.440 --> 21:11.840
who with great ingenuity daily meet the challenge of an untold variety of tastes and needs in

21:11.840 --> 21:18.740
hospital food. And the army public health nurse who works with military personnel and

21:18.740 --> 21:24.240
their families in keeping well people well and in nursing the sick back to health. Among

21:24.240 --> 21:33.240
their responsibilities are providing prenatal care, assisting diabetics, and in following

21:33.240 --> 21:41.440
up on the full recovery of TB patients. When you go over in your mind as I did mother,

21:41.440 --> 21:46.640
all that had taken place in such a short span of time, you realize many things. I realized

21:46.640 --> 21:51.140
that I had learned something new about nursing and medicine every day I had spent as an army

21:51.140 --> 21:56.240
nurse. That I was part of an organization made up of stimulating people who were intent

21:56.240 --> 22:01.340
on saving lives and on finding new cures. People who constantly provided me with the

22:01.340 --> 22:06.880
widest horizons both of the mind and the spirit. And I suspected that army nursing was no longer

22:06.880 --> 22:11.840
a means to an end for me as it had been at the beginning, but a way of life.

22:11.840 --> 22:22.240
Is this a private seance or is anyone invited? Paul, I didn't hear you. I was just being

22:22.240 --> 22:29.040
my usual quiet and reserved self. How did you know I was here? I just said to myself

22:29.040 --> 22:37.740
now where would she be if she wasn't in her usual haunts? Right here. Still meditating

22:37.740 --> 22:46.980
the big question? Mm-hmm. Any luck? I think so. Anyway, I've been doing a lot of thinking

22:46.980 --> 22:54.200
about things I haven't thought very much about before. Meaning me, I hope. Now look, Ruth,

22:54.200 --> 22:59.320
why don't you do what I've asked you to do, what, 50 or 100 times? Why not just up and

22:59.320 --> 23:03.280
marry me and chuck the rest of the problem right in that pool there? I bet your mother

23:03.280 --> 23:16.440
would like that. No go, huh? Oh, I can't do that. Paul, I love you. I just don't think

23:16.440 --> 23:23.800
that marriage is necessarily the answer to any problem. Yep, I guess you're right. And

23:23.800 --> 23:29.000
much as I hate to, I have to agree with you. Well, as long as you keep your promise to

23:29.000 --> 23:36.080
marry me, I'll just have to go along. You know what's troubling you, Ruth? I do. Because

23:36.080 --> 23:42.120
you're a lot like me. You're ambitious. You started your nursing career with practically

23:42.120 --> 23:46.960
nothing. And now you're not only well on your way to a master's degree, but to becoming

23:46.960 --> 23:52.000
a full-fledged expert in psychiatric nursing. And you're afraid you'll lose both goals if

23:52.000 --> 23:58.240
you quit the service now. Say, you're not planning to go on for a medical degree and

23:58.240 --> 24:05.720
become a doctor, are you? No, silly. One doctor in this family is quite enough. Well, that's

24:05.720 --> 24:11.360
a comfort. I can see us both competing for the same practice. Well, anyway, where was

24:11.360 --> 24:20.120
I? Oh, yes, I was saying that you're very much like me. Ruth, we both suffer from an

24:20.120 --> 24:27.320
inner drive that just won't let us rest. A drive that can best be diagnosed as an insatiable

24:27.320 --> 24:33.200
hunger for new knowledge, a new experience. Of course, not all people are like that, but

24:33.200 --> 24:39.960
we are. My mother and father both find it very difficult to understand why I prefer

24:39.960 --> 24:44.720
to practice medicine in the Army. Well, for now at least, to any practice I might have

24:44.720 --> 24:50.480
in civilian life. Ruth, they just don't fathom the tremendous satisfaction you and I get

24:50.480 --> 24:56.960
out of meeting new people, making new and lasting friendships, seeing new places, meeting

24:56.960 --> 25:12.520
new challenges. Not only in this country, but in such places as Lebanon and the Philippines.

25:12.520 --> 25:16.800
They can't appreciate our sitting and brooding about the fascination of the work to be done

25:16.800 --> 25:30.280
in Korea, or Puerto Rico, or Japan, or wherever the vital interests of our country should

25:30.280 --> 25:41.560
demand our presence. That's an important key to us, Ruth. Strange as it may sound to some,

25:41.560 --> 25:47.200
you and I are the kind of people who strongly believe in doing something important and worthwhile

25:47.200 --> 25:52.000
for our country, wherever it takes us. Now you believe in that as strongly as I do. I

25:52.000 --> 25:57.200
know. I've watched your face as some of us have talked about the deep satisfaction we

25:57.200 --> 26:02.120
got from our work and experience in distant places. And now you see yourself adding to

26:02.120 --> 26:18.320
your personal and broad educational experience in such places as Paris and Rome. Beautiful,

26:18.320 --> 26:32.720
beautiful Rome. Hawaii. Or any one of a dozen other intriguing places around the world.

26:32.720 --> 26:37.240
Paul of course was right. Both he and I were people who thought less of serving our own

26:37.240 --> 26:42.800
purposes than we did of serving others, wherever we were needed. Neither of us, we knew, could

26:42.800 --> 26:51.720
be happy any other way. And so, Mother, right at this moment, I just can't bring myself

26:51.720 --> 26:57.760
to do what I know you hope I will do. I can't leave this work I've come to know and love,

26:57.760 --> 27:04.160
at least not yet. That doesn't mean I love you any less, or miss you any less, or want

27:04.160 --> 27:10.920
to be near you any less. What it only means is that I find, at the moment, that being

27:10.920 --> 27:16.120
an Army nurse is being something very special. I have yet to hear of another place where

27:16.120 --> 27:21.280
nurses are as much the doctor's right hand, his counsel and his confidence, his extra

27:21.280 --> 27:26.060
eyes and ears as we who are in the Corps. Even the patients we treat have a special

27:26.060 --> 27:32.680
regard for our being what we are. I find it very gratifying. And the rank we hold, Lieutenant,

27:32.680 --> 27:38.760
Captain, Major and higher, makes us something even more special. Right now, Mother dearest,

27:38.760 --> 27:46.120
I just can't give any of it up. I hope you will understand. I plan to visit you very

27:46.120 --> 28:15.160
soon. Until then, and with all my love, your daughter, Ruth.

28:16.120 --> 28:22.160
